   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34)\">Hi everyone,</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34)\">I&#39;m using readModels to extract the modification indices from a multi-group graded response model. However, mod_indices does not contain the modification indices for the individual thresholds. For example, in my Mplus output: <u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34)\">Means/Intercepts/Thresholds<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34)\">[ NARQ1    ]                      24.991     0.215      0.215        0.178<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34)\">[ NARQ3    ]                      23.250    -0.297     -0.297       -0.202<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34)\">[ NARQ5    ]                      78.514     0.404      0.404        0.336<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34)\">[ NARQ16   ]                      44.555    -0.911     -0.911       -0.334<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34)\">[ NARQ1$1  ]                       7.538    -0.143     -0.143       -0.119<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34)\">[ NARQ1$2  ]                       2.882    -0.109     -0.109       -0.091<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34)\">[ NARQ1$3  ]                       5.636    -0.163     -0.163       -0.135<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34)\">[ NARQ1$4  ]                       3.380    -0.108     -0.108       -0.089<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34)\">With readModels, only the modification indices for the item intercepts are extracted, but not the ones for the individual thresholds (NARQ1$1 - NARQ1$4). Is there any way to obtain the modification indices for the thresholds within MplusAutomation? <u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34)\">Any help with this would be greatly appreciated!<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34)\">Best wishes,<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34)\">Eunike<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div>"
